// HTTP/3, RFC 9114:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114
//
// The frame layer of §7.1 and §7.2 with the placement rules that say which frame may
// arrive on which stream, the settings of §7.2.4, the unidirectional stream types of
// §6.2, a request and a response as field sections, and the connection state an endpoint
// keeps while the two control streams find each other.
//
// Header compression is `qpack` and the frame lengths are written in the variable-length
// integer of `varint`. The QUIC transport underneath is `moonquic`, which this package
// never names: a frame layer reads bytes, and where they came from is the caller's.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonvar/quic",
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/qpack",
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/header",
}
